.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::OutputRegionsToGoCadFiles (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sgroup, const char * property, long timestep = \fR0\fP) const"
Depending on whether the CSMP model is either two- or three-dimensional, \fBOutputRegionsToGoCadFiles()\fP output the target variable from all \fBRegion\fP subregions inside the model to GoCad TSurf or GoCad TSolid files, respectively\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The first argument gives the name of the output physical variable and the second argument depicts the current timestep in a transient CSMP simulation\&. This timestep will be appended to the output filename before the GoCad specific file extension ('\&.ts' for TSurf and '\&.so' for TSolid files)\&. The names of the output files will be composed of the \fBRegion\fP names inside the CSP model and the name of the physical variable using a hyphen as separator, for instance\&. 
.br

.PP
granite-pressure1\&.ts
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Method depends of the \fBRegion\fP interfaces '\fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP' and '\fBOutputVariableToTSolid()\fP'\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
\fBOutputRegionsToGoCadFiles()\fP presents a very convinient way to output selected subregions of a CSP model as GoCad input files for visualisation\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report an error and exit without completing its task, if no \fBRegion\fP objects were defined in the model\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::OutputVariablesToTSurface (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sgroup, const char * fname, long timestep = \fR0\fP) const"
Uses the \fBModel\fP method \fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP to output all the variables of a current model to a GoCad TSurf file with the extension '\&.ts'\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The name of the output file and the model timestep for which the variables shall be reported\&. The timestep will be appended to the filename before the extension '\&.ts'\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
Uses the \fBModel\fP method \fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP to output individual variables\&. Please to refer to its documentation for further implementation details\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Externalize the property values of a run to visualize them in GoCad\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report errors if the output file cannot be opened, if no physical variables are defined or if the model is not two-dimensional\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::OutputVariableToTSolid (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sgroup, const char * fname, const char * group_name, const char * var, long timestep = \fR0\fP) const"
Given a three-dimensional CSMP model, \fBOutputVariableToTSolid()\fP creates a GoCad TSolid dataset for the indicated variable in a subregion of the model which was previously identified as a \fBRegion\fP object\&. The variable is to a textfile with the GoCad specific extension '\&.so'\&. The TSolid format is described in the GoCad manual, Appendix B (p\&. B-14) and consists of:

.PP
GoCad header, PVTRX list: node coordinate and property data listed by node number, TETRA list: nodes per tetrahedral finite element, END end of file specifier

.PP
Importantly, a TSolid file written by GoCad will contain constraint point lists preceding each TETRA block\&. In constrast to CSMP jargon, a constraint point in GoCad is a node point which lies on an object boundary\&. In this fashion, the model volume is described object by object\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSolid()\fP expects four arguments, the last is the timestep in a simulation which is represented by the dataset\&. This argument is optional\&. The first argument is the name of the file to which the TSolid dataset is written to and to whose name the timestep is appended\&. If the timestep is not specified, a zero will be appended to the filename before the extension '\&.so'\&. The second argument is the name of the group object defining the model subregion over which the variable (third argument) shall be output\&. 
.br
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The method uses a \fBGocadHeader\fP class object to write the file and the property class header in the TSolid file\&.

.PP
If the method is used to output element properties, these will be mapped onto the nodes, since GoCad only permits nodal variables\&. To achieve the mapping, intermediate variable vectors are created and all nodes of each element are assigned the corresponding element property value\&. This strategy has the disadvantage that nodes with a higher ID number will overwrite the property values on nodes with lower numbers\&. The effect may be a rugged appearance of element property boundaries\&. User suggestions are welcome to overcome this deficiency\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The method is used to output a property to a TSolid representing a subregion of a CSMP model\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report an error and fail to write an output file, if it cannot open the specified file with extension '\&.so' in text mode\&.

.PP
If the target group is not defined (which it may due to a spelling error, for instance), the method will also report this as an error\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::OutputVariableToTSolid (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sgroup, const char * fname, const char * var, long timestep = \fR0\fP) const"
Given a three-dimensional CSMP model, \fBOutputVariableToTSolid()\fP creates a GoCad TSolid dataset for the indicated variable and output it to a textfile with the GoCad specific extension '\&.so'\&. The TSolid format is described in the GoCad manual, Appendix B (p\&. B-14) and consists of:

.PP
GoCad header, PVTRX list: node coordinate and property data listed by node number, TETRA list: nodes per tetrahedral finite element, END end of file specifier

.PP
Importantly, a TSolid file written by GoCad will contain constraint point lists preceding each TETRA block\&. In this fashion, the model volume is described object by object\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSolid()\fP expects three arguments, the third of which is the timestep in a simulation which is represented by the dataset\&. This argument is optional\&. The first argument is the name of the file to which the TSolid dataset is written to and to whose name the timestep is appended to\&. If the timestep is not specified, a zero will be appended to the filename before the extension '\&.so'\&. The second argument defines the variable which shall be output to file\&. 
.br
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The method uses the \fBGocadHeader\fP object to write the file and the property class header for the TSolid file\&.

.PP
If the method is used to output element properties, these will be mapped onto the nodes, since GoCad only permits nodal variables\&. To achieve the mapping, intermediate variable vectors are created and all nodes of each element are assigned the corresponding element property value\&. This strategy has the disadvantage that nodes with a higher ID number will overwrite the property values on nodes with lower numbers\&. The effect may be a rugged appearance of element property boundaries\&. User suggestions are welcome to overcome this deficiency\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The method is used to output a property to a TSolid for an entire- as opposed to a region of a CSMP model\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method will report an error and fail to write an output file, if it cannot open the specified file with extension '\&.so' in text mode\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::OutputVariableToTSurface (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sgroup, const char * fname, const char * group_name, const char * var, long timestep = \fR0\fP) const"
Outputs a physical variable in \fBRegion\fP subregions of the \fBModel\fP to a GoCad TSurf object which is stored into a textfile with the recommended extension '\&.ts' for direct import into GoCad as GoCad object\&.

.PP
The GoCad TSurf format is defined in Appendix B of the GoCad manual (p\&. B-10)\&. In brief, it is a list of the following items:

.PP
a GoCad header, PVTRX information: vertex coordinates and associated property values, TRGL triangle connectivity information: the numbers of nodes in each triangle, END the end of file marker\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP takes four arguments, the name of the output file to which the fourth argument which is the timestep and the extension '\&.ts' are appended\&. The second argument specifies the name of the \fBRegion\fP subregion of the model and the third argument indicates the variable which shall be output to file\&. Thus far, if variables 
.br
 are element variables they will still be stored on the nodes in the output file\&. This may cause boundary nodes of regions appear oddly valued, since the element node values will overlap with eachother depending on the node numbering in the model\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP uses several atomistic class objects to represent gocad formats, these are the \fBGocadHeader\fP and the \fBGocadPropertyClassHeader\fP objects\&.

.PP
The method only works for two-dimensional models\&. 3D models must be output as GoCad TSolid objects (see corresponding documentation)\&.

.PP
IntegrationPoint variables cannot be output to TSurf files\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP provides a direct interface to the GoCad visualization and modeling program\&. Use it to visualize scalar or vector variables in GoCad\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
If the output file cannot be opened, if the model is not two-dimensional, if the target \fBRegion\fP is not defined, or if an attempt is made to output a IntegrationPoint variable, the method will report an error and exit without completing its task\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::OutputVariableToTSurface (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & sgroup, const char * fname, const char * var, long timestep = \fR0\fP) const"

.PP
output of data from CSMP to GoCad Outputs a physical variable from the \fBModel\fP to a GoCad TSurf object which is stored into a textfile with the recommended extension '\&.ts' for direct import into GoCad as GoCad object\&.

.PP
The GoCad TSurf format is defined in Appendix B of the GoCad manual (p\&. B-10)\&. In brief, it is a list of the following items:

.PP
a GoCad header, PVTRX information: vertex coordinates and associated property values, TRGL triangle connectivity information: the numbers of nodes in each triangle, END the end of file marker\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP takes three arguments, the name of the output file to which the third argument which is the timestep and the extension '\&.ts' are appended\&. The second argument specifies the variable which is output to file\&. Thus far, if variables 
.br
 are element variables they will still be stored on the nodes in the output file\&. This may cause boundary nodes of regions appear oddly valued, since the element node values will overlap with eachother depending on the node numbering in the model\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP uses several atomistic class objects to represent gocad formats, these are the \fBGocadHeader\fP and the \fBGocadPropertyClassHeader\fP objects\&.

.PP
The method only works for two-dimensional models\&. 3D models must be output as GoCad TSolid objects (see corresponding documentation)\&.

.PP
IntegrationPoint variables cannot be output to TSurf files\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
\fBOutputVariableToTSurface()\fP provides a direct interface to the GoCad visualization and modeling program\&. Use it to visualize scalar or vector variables in GoCad\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
If the output file cannot be opened, if the model is not two-dimensional, or if an attempt is made to output a IntegrationPoint variable, the method will report an error and exit without completing its task\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::ReadTetrahedralGocad3DMesh (const char * file, \fBGocadHeader\fP & header, \fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset)"
Top level method to read ASCII text files from the geometric modeling program GoCad which were output in the TSolid format\&. The method just reads the header of the GoCad file diagnosing its format and interpreting which datasets are contained\&. If the file header can be interpreted correctly, control is transferred to ReadTSolid() which will read the data from the TSolid file\&.

.PP
ReadGocadText() expects either no variable or the variable 'permeability' to be specified in the GoCad output file\&. At the moment, the method only supports the reading of a single property\&. Thus, if the file contains multiple properties, the reading process will fail\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The name of the GoCaD text, ascii file with the TSolid description, a GoCadHeader object which will store the information about the GoCad dataset, and the \fBVSet\fP into which the information from the GoCad file will be returned\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvset\fP The mesh and associated data from the TSolid dataset will be returned into the \fBVSet\fP supplied as third method argument\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The method parses the values of the GoCad variables PROPERTIES, PROPERTY_CLASSES, and ESIZES (dimensions of each variable) and starts the method ReadTSolid() with the according input arguments\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
The methods provides an interface to the GoCaD geometric modeling tool, facilitating that tetrahedral meshes created by this program can be used in CSMP computations\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
If the GoCad input file does not exist, if more than a single property was specified therein, or if the variable 'permeability' is missing the method will report an error and exit\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::GoCadInterface\fP< dim >::ReadTetrahedralGocad3DSurface (const char * fname, \fBGocadHeader\fP & header, \fBVSet\fP< dim > & vset)"

.PP
input of data from GoCad to CSMP Reads the GoCad header and property class headers from the input text file created by GoCad\&. The method subsequently calls ReadTSurface() which reads the actual data from the input file and puts them into the supplied \fBVSet\fP, including property data if present\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The first argument specifies the input file name without (\&.ts) extension which is appended automatically\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIheader\fP The second method argument is used to store the header information which is retrieved from the input file,
.br
\fIvset\fP the third argument will hold the mesh which was read, including the property data if such were present\&. 
.br
.RE
.PP
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
To read GoCad 'TSurf' surfaces with assigned properties from textfiles output by GoCad\&. 
.br
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The method reports the information given in the header section of the GoCad file\&. This includes the header with the object type and name, as well as the property class headers for the properties associated with the surface\&. 

